WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:06.379
Carole Kirschner: If you have an idea that
could be on the show, that’s not quite good

00:00:06.379 --> 00:00:09.080
enough.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:14.919
It should be something that fits in, that
captures the voice and tone of the show, but

00:00:14.919 --> 00:00:18.140
goes a little beyond what they do.

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:24.668
My favorite, favorite spec concept was for
Cheers [TV series that ran from 1982 to 1993]

00:00:24.668 --> 00:00:27.270
which most of your viewers will not know anything
about.

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:28.270
Film Courage: I loved it!

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:30.000
Carole Kirschner: I loved it.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.470
So in real life The Pope came to Boston where
that show is set.

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:43.290
And The Guy in White went down the main street
in his Pope-mobile and in this spec The Pope

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:46.550
goes to Cheers [the bar in the tv show] because
he has to use the bathroom.

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:53.390
So The Pope goes into the bathroom, leaves,
and people are just stunned that The Pope

00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:57.720
came and used their bathroom and then somebody
steals the toilet.

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:03.580
The thing about it is, it’s a funny concept
and it was a way to show each of the main

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:07.940
characters, what their views on religion and
spirituality were.

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:14.000
So any time you can pick a concept where you
reveal more about the characters, the better.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.831
Film Courage: Okay, so if you know let’s
suppose Silicon Valley is the show that you

00:01:18.831 --> 00:01:19.831
love.

00:01:19.831 --> 00:01:23.490
And you know these characters would definitely
do this and I can totally see this working,

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:25.170
that’s almost a negative?

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:28.890
Carole Kirschner: No, no, it’s not a negative.

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:34.170
That’s the starting point, is that this
is accurate, this is something that fits into

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:35.500
this world.

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:39.250
And then you try something that pushes it
a little bit.

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:40.560
Not aliens are landing.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:43.090
That’s a really bad idea.

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:47.550
You want to stay with the reality of the world,
but just go deeper.

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:50.840
Find something deeper about the character.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:59.560
And I once said on a podcast start your script
with affairs, passing on or greed.

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:00.560
They always work.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:03.159
Grab people’s attention with one of those
things.

